+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4341 as an offline, no-leaderboard E3 explore-verify-plan reproduction attempt on provisional `sc25`, using `results/arc_e3/sc25/world_model.py` as the induced executable world-model deliverable and reusing the stalled BFS solver's replay-from-reset, warm-up-after-reset, corrected cast-grid coordinates `(24+5c,49+5r)`, tank-control facing state, and fireball-animation resolution gotchas. It MUST first confirm that `environment_files/sc25/` is non-empty, that `python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py` and `python/carnot/agentic/arc_solver_kit.py` import, that TRM training is stood down, and that `scripts/research_conductor.py` is not modified; if the sc25 offline simulator is missing it MUST write `honest_verdict="blocked_offline_env_missing_sc25"` and stop without leaderboard submission. The workflow MUST collect offline sc25 transitions with the sc25 replay/cast wiring, record verifier-gated transition lemmas for the spell-cast, cast-grid, and tank-control mechanics before planning, run adaptive unit probes for the fireball-animation and cast-pattern-clear hidden rules, print and persist `verifier_accuracy_per_round`, and plan only after the model has passed the bounded mechanic checks. A solve SHALL be accepted only when the induced-model plan executes through the real offline environment without visible-mechanic divergence and `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` reports at least one offline-reproduced level. If the bounded round budget ends without such a reproduced solve, it MUST write an honest partial artifact with the best verifier accuracy and classify the residual as a missing-world-model-rule gap for `sc25`. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4341_e3_sc25_reproduction.json` MUST include `honest_verdict`, `verifier_accuracy_per_round`, `win_mechanic_cracked`, `world_model_path`, `world_model_sha256`, `offline_reproduced`, `reproduced_levels`, `verifier_is_oracle`, `preconditions_checked`, `random_seed`, and `reproducibility_checksum`, with `win_mechanic_cracked`, `offline_reproduced`, `reproduced_levels`, and `verifier_is_oracle` emitted as bare values rather than principle-wrapped dictionaries. The artifact field principles SHALL be exactly: `honest_verdict` = `Terminal-prefixed (success_e3_sc25_L1_reproduced or complete_e3_sc25_partial_model_<acc>). A reproduced L1 (the first reproducible sc25 level, opening the path to +5) and an honest partial (induced model + win-mechanic gap) are BOTH progress.`; `verifier_accuracy_per_round` = `list[float]: the verifier's reproduction rate per refactor round on sc25's complex mechanic.`; `win_mechanic_cracked` = `BARE bool: did the induced model capture a complete win path (player-to-exit OR cast-grid alignment) the BFS solver could not? -- the diagnostic for whether E3 unblocks where BFS stalled.`; `world_model_path` = `results/arc_e3/sc25/world_model.py -- the induced model IS the deliverable.`; `world_model_sha256` = `Hash of the induced world model -- auditable/reproducible.`; `offline_reproduced` = `BARE bool: the real env reaches L1 via the induced-model plan, re-gated -- only reproduced levels count (sc25's 5 levels are LIVE-RECORDED, NOT reproduced -- this is the gate that converts them).`; `reproduced_levels` = `BARE int: levels offline-reproduced on sc25 (target >=1) -- the +1 unit, opening the path to the 5 live-recorded levels.`; `verifier_is_oracle` = `BARE bool=true -- the SOLVE is execution-grounded (real env defines the win); ARC progress, NOT a moat headline.`; `preconditions_checked` = `Records the offline-env presence + harness import + TRM-stand-down; pre-empts the silent-missing-resource fabrication mode.`; `random_seed` = `Determinism precondition for the induction + exploration + planning.`; `reproducibility_checksum` = `Hash of the world model + the plan + the reproduce() result; lets a third party re-run.`
